PATCH 472: the remaining node-kind renderers 29ec (kind 2) / 30de (kind 0xa) / 2bb8 (kind 4) and their
size-override wrappers 309b (kind 8) / 30bc (kind 0xc) (windshield-object frontier, slice 8).

All three share 2e49's prologue (patch 471: gates, 0e22 scale, 3e8c/405e/3e29/400b/3ed4).  29ec (asm
0x29ec-0x2b93) uses one descriptor (facing from 059a(word[bx+8])) whose segment 0x6b5c serves the whole
list; 30de (0x30de-0x3281) takes the facing directly as (word[bx+8]&0x1f)<<1; 2bb8 (0x2bb8-0x2e44) has a
BASE descriptor (059a(byte[bx+0x32]<<8) -> 0x6b64/0x6b66) whose single polygon list seeds the sorted list
and a PART descriptor (059a(word[bx+8]) -> 0x6ad8/0x6ada) for the part facings at node+0x33, re-touching
each descriptor in the walk and taking es from it.  The abort helpers 2b94/3282/2e45 (`pop ax; pop bx;
ret`) return from the renderer.  309b/30bc swap the per-code size word[0x27b0+code] with word[node+0x32+
cnt] around 29ec/30de (`xchg`, restored after).  Each polygon posts op-0x40 through e132 with the
patch-471 register lanes.  Ghidra host-deref'd the node/descriptors/resource tables (SEGV in 309b once
2e49 landed).
